       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That's twice the usual maximum for adults, which is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. A dose that high carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nThe dose may be a typo. Possible intended orders include:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **1700 mg/day**, for example 850 mg twice daily.\n- **500 mg or 1000 mg** per dose, at a different frequency.\n\nPlease confirm the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If 1700 mg three times daily is really intended, for example as part of a specific protocol, tell me and I'll enter it with a note documenting that you confirmed it. I'd suggest checking with pharmacy first."
